            <ArticleTitle>The comparative in vitro activity of relebactam, imipenem and the combination of the two, plus six comparator antimicrobial agents against 432 strains of anaerobic organisms including imipenem-resistant strains.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">AAC.01992-17</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1128/AAC.01992-17</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Relebactam is an important beta-lactamase inhibitor for certain aerobic organisms but alone it has no anti-anaerobic activity, with most anaerobes having MICs ≥32 μg/ml with the exception of a very few strains. There was no enhancement or antagonism of imipenem activity with the addition of relebactam, including activity against imipenem resistant strains. The relebactam-imipenem combination had excellent overall activity against the anaerobes tested.</AbstractText>
